[description]

[b]Pull requests[/b] in Azure Repos behave like other forges: diff, threads, iteration on pushes, and merge when policies pass. [b]Branch policies[/b] can require reviewers, successful builds, linked work items, and comment resolution—stack policies carefully so contributors understand the minimum bar.

[b]Work item links:[/b] associating a PR with Boards items helps release notes and audits; requiring links can slow tiny fixes—teams sometimes exempt hotfix branches.

[b]Iteration fields:[/b] Azure DevOps tracks iteration paths separately from Git branches—keep naming aligned to reduce confusion in sprint reviews.

[b]Takeaway:[/b] PRs are the negotiation layer; policies encode what “done” means before Git moves the protected ref.
